WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:03.003
The hardest thing for me is that

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.771
I never got to say goodbye

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.506
to my old life.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.209
I was an avid rock climber.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.410
I worked out every day.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.612
I ate extremely healthy.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.947
There was really nothing

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:14.881
that I could have done

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.550
to prevent what happened

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.752
a little over a year ago.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:22.322
I was hospitalized with COVID

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.493
I was born with aortic valve stenosis.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.561
I wasn't able to do sports at all.

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:29.596
I wasn't really allowed

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:31.931
to do a lot of workouts

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.533
I wasn't allowed to run.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.435
So with my heart,

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:37.504
it did make it a little bit worse.

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.073
I flatlined three times a quickly.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.842
My state started to become really bad.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.878
I found to psychosis.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.580
I had my legs amputated.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.884
I lost £70 because I wasn't able to eat

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:51.851
or drink

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.319
There were certain,

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:53.853
you know,

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.221
life support systems that they couldn't

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.090
put me on because of my heart.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.291
I was in the hospital

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.460
recovering for two months in a day.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.361
I mean, there were

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.462
some days that I was like,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.130
oh, you know, in a year I'll be good.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.066
But most days I was like,

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.133
I don't even know if I'm going to make

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.101
it till tomorrow.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.371
Normally it will take

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:12.806
more energy to walk

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.275
with prosthetics than not.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:16.009
I did it.

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:16.976
And on top

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.279
of not having any muscle to begin with,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.181
it was just overexerting

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.082
and my heart

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:25.051
not being taught to your condition.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.252
It just made everyday

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.355
activities extremely difficult to do

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.431
It takes

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.265
three months

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.901
post-surgery to be fully recovered.

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.470
This will actually be the first time

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.971
that I can run

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.274
long distance or trains for that period.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:49.209
Go.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:52.345
I'll be able to climb

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.181
proficiently post-COVID

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.450
for the first time. Got it clear.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.419
So I have finally

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.254
able to start modeling again.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.355
When I look at the pictures,

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.156
i see the beauty.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.090
I see the

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.492
the strength, the resilience,

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:07.327
and that ain't gonna take.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:07.827
No.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:11.131
I definitely looked back

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:14.601
on my old pictures and I would 100%

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:15.702
compare them to now.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.604
It's kind of hard to not.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:18.338
But then I remember

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.140
I look at like Aimee Mullins

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.175
and you heard the word Wasser,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:25.812
and I'm like, well, they look great.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.881
I mean, there's only one way to go

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.015
and it's forward.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.817
Can't really go anywhere else and.

